The Czix project is a free, unofficial application launcher made to run the
Roblox Android client on Linux. It is an unofficial community project; it does
not generate any revenue for its authors whatsoever.

Czix is completely unaffiliated with Roblox or its partners. Czix is not
affiliated with Google, Android, or the Android Open Source Project.

Czix does not redistribute any part of Roblox's intellectual property or code.
Instead, Czix downloads the Roblox Application Bundle (APK) directly from a
public mirror of the officially published application (APKPure, Internet
Archive), and verifies its signing certificate before installing it. Users are
responsible for their own downloads — Czix is only a delivery and trust
machinery for a file the user could download themselves, pinned to the official
signer for safety.

Given Czix's experimental nature, and given Roblox does NO testing or quality
assurance for Czix clients, there is a chance that using it can lead to a
broken experience or an account suspension (third-party clients are a Terms of
Service gray area for most platforms). You use Czix at your own risk.

The Czix project does not support any misuse of Roblox systems or platforms;
cheating, exploiting, or bypassing payment systems are strictly out of scope
for this project and its community.

Czix is not endorsed by any of the projects, persons, or companies listed above.
